E2  kernel identity: linear-response tensors for a point mass in a uniform field (own derivation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  QUMOND (Poisson-solved): Phi_Q(k) = nu0 (1 + L k_z^2/k^2) Phi_N(k), L = dln nu/dln y at the Newtonian external field y_e.
    real space: Phi_Q = -GM nu0 [ (1 + L/2)/r - (L/2) z^2/r^3 ]  =>  radial boost B_r(theta) = nu0 [1 + (L/2) sin^2 theta]; B_par = nu0, B_perp = nu0 (1 + L/2); sphere average nu0 (1 + L/3).
  AQUAL: operator mu0 [lap + L0 d_z^2] phi = 4 pi G rho with L0 = dln mu/dln x (x = observed field/a0); rescaled Green's function gives B_par = 1/mu0 = nu0, B_perp = nu0/sqrt(1+L0).
  algebraic / local (MI-type) tensor: perpendicular perturbation nu0, parallel perturbation d(y nu)/dy = nu0 (1+L).
  [PASS] E2a sympy: lap(r) = 2/r, so F^-1[1/k^4] = -r/(8 pi) solves lap f = -1/(4 pi r)*(... ) as used (checks the k_z^2/k^4 -> (1/8pi)(1/r - z^2/r^3) step)
